From e8d6f4823df6a1b9afef2fff121945b81cca87fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mouhamed Bassiroou Khouma <Mouhamedbk1002@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:52:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): replace Manus OAuth with Google OAuth

- server/_core/googleAuth.ts: new Google token exchange + userinfo client (native fetch, no new dep)
- server/_core/oauth.ts: /api/oauth/callback now talks to Google instead of Manus's WebDevAuthPublicService
- server/_core/sdk.ts: strip Manus OAuthService/exchangeCodeForToken/getUserInfoWithJwt and the cron-openId bypass; keep only the provider-agnostic JWT session (create/sign/verify) used by both Google login and the existing local admin login
- server/_core/env.ts: drop OAUTH_SERVER_URL/VITE_APP_ID/VITE_OAUTH_PORTAL_URL, add GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET/GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI
- client/src/const.ts: startLogin() now redirects straight to Google's consent screen instead of the Manus app-auth portal
- client/src/main.tsx, useAuth.ts: drop manus-cookie/manus-runtime-user-info (Manus preview-iframe specific), rely on the first-party session cookie
- remove server/_core/types/manusTypes.ts (no longer referenced)
- users are now keyed as openId = google:<sub>, loginMethod = 'google'
